\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Proposition}
\title{One free Hurwitz coefficient per based cell}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{For the \vocabk{internal right action}{fdip-00VK}, put
#{r=2^n|X|}. The cochain module is free of right
#{\mathcal O_k}-rank #{r} and of #{k}-rank #{4r}:
##{C^\bullet(X;\mathcal O_k)\cong\mathcal O_k^r.}
Every #{\extD_U} is right #{\mathcal O_k}-linear.
The internal commutant of the left #{2T} action on one
coefficient is #{\mathcal O_k^{\mathrm{op}}}.}

\proof{
\p{A based cell is specified by #{x\in X} and an exterior
subset #{I}. The cochain which is #{1} on that cell
and zero elsewhere is a right-module basis vector:
every cochain has its unique expansion with the
corresponding Hurwitz coefficients. There are
#{2^n|X|} such cells. Expanding each coefficient in
#{(1,\qi,\qj,h)} gives #{4r} vectors in a #{k}-basis.}

\p{Each forward or inverse link is left multiplication on
the coefficient. It commutes with right multiplication;
the exterior operations and site sums also commute with
it. This proves right linearity of the displayed
cochain operator. The coefficient commutant is
\ref{fdip-00V5}: the group contains the basis
#{1,\qi,\qj,h}, so commuting with it means commuting
with every left multiplication. Evaluation at #{1}
then determines exactly a right multiplication.}
}
